{title=Mutual information for the two Bell-label positions and for known or forgotten bit positions}
{description=Original calculations for independent fair input bits, Bell-readout error $1/5$, and the labeling in the solution. The first bit may flip while the second is noiseless. Knowing which position a bit occupies retains more information than pooling the two channels and discarding that label.}
